WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.233 --> 00:00:03.984
Can AI reveal useful clues to pulmonary embolism

2
00:00:04.006 --> 00:00:06.252
from a CT scan without contrast?

3
00:00:06.965 --> 00:00:10.195
A generative adversarial network learns from paired scans,

4
00:00:10.310 --> 00:00:11.954
creates synthetic enhancement,

5
00:00:12.185 --> 00:00:14.616
and feeds a pulmonary embolism classifier.

6
00:00:15.270 --> 00:00:19.380
The retrospective evaluation included forty-three internal patients

7
00:00:19.599 --> 00:00:22.100
and sixty-two patients from another hospital.

8
00:00:22.754 --> 00:00:26.123
With synthetic images, internal patient-level AUC

9
00:00:26.215 --> 00:00:28.716
reached zero point eight three six.

10
00:00:29.393 --> 00:00:33.249
In the external cohort, it fell to zero point six eight zero.

11
00:00:33.456 --> 00:00:35.216
Real contrast scored higher.

12
00:00:35.940 --> 00:00:39.472
Patient models used cross-validation within each cohort.

13
00:00:39.713 --> 00:00:42.400
Small samples do not establish equivalence.

14
00:00:43.042 --> 00:00:46.492
A promising direction: learn more from noncontrast CT.

15
00:00:46.862 --> 00:00:48.807
Validate before clinical use.
